          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-24T22:29:00-07:00",
          "message": "fix(config): the editor and the loader read a config file by one rule, so an edit reads back as written (candybar-law-review-ibyq.562)\n\nA text that holds nothing but whitespace and comments is no document to\neither reader, refused in one set of words: read as an empty object, it is\nwhat an editor's in-place rewrite shows between its truncate and its write,\nand a click landing there would replace the file the editor is still\nwriting. A layer with no file starts from the empty document, and a click on\na file the editor refuses is refused naming the file.\n\nAn insert into an object holding only a comment keeps the comment. A `//`\ncomment ends at every line terminator JSON5 ends it at. Save-as-preset reads\nthe layers above through the loader's syntax stage.\n"
        }
